# For assignment context, I should use expand_word_unquoted behavior for non-quoted parts

# Let me look at how the Word is structured for x=$(echo "hello world")
# The parser would create: Word { parts: [CmdSub(...)], quoted: false }
# If x="$(echo "hello world")", it would be: Word { parts: [...], quoted: true }

# So the fix is: in expand_to_string, for non-quoted words, use unquoted expansion for the CmdSub
# But also, the result from unquoted expansion should be joined without spaces

# Actually, looking at nsh behavior again:
# x=$(echo "a b c") -> x=abc (all whitespace stripped)
# x="$(echo "a b c")" -> x="a b c" (preserved)
# x=$a where a="a b c" -> x=abc (all whitespace stripped)
# x="$a" where a="a b c" -> x="a b c" (preserved)

